## 🚀 DEPLOYMENT INSTRUCTIONS

### Step 1: Create Project Folder
```bash
mkdir heeco-website
cd heeco-website
```

### Step 2: Create All Folders
```bash
mkdir pages components styles public
mkdir public/images
```

### Step 3: Copy All Files
Copy each file content from above into the respective location in your project folder.

### Step 4: Install Dependencies
```bash
npm install
```

### Step 5: Test Locally
```bash
npm run dev
```
Visit http://localhost:3000 to see your site!

### Step 6: Build for Production
```bash
npm run build
```
This creates an `out/` folder with static HTML files.

### Step 7: Deploy to Netlify

**Option A: Drag & Drop (Easiest)**
1. Go to https://app.netlify.com
2. Drag the entire `out/` folder to the deploy area
3. Done! Your site is live

**Option B: Git Deploy (Recommended)**
```bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"
git remote add origin YOUR_REPO_URL
git push -u origin main
```

Then in Netlify:
1. Click "Add new site"
2. Connect to Git
3. Select your repository
4. Build settings are auto-detected from netlify.toml
5. Click "Deploy site"

